    "original_reconstruction": "The unchanged whole-module formal reconstruction covers 45 source declarations, including four private helpers, and all literal definitions, domains and proof mechanisms. A chronological little-endian RY/CX circuit recursively prepares low-wire marginal norms, then splits the new highest wire with an exact signed polar angle. Its generic first-column theorem requires a pointwise nonnegative real table and positive actual sum of squares; the flat little-endian wrapper assumes strict positivity. The zero-input column is exactly f/sqrt(sum f^2), not merely equal up to phase. Signed pair recovery is total, while the stated generic preparation theorem retains its sign restriction, including at zero width. Counts are exactly 2^n-1 RY and 2*(2^n-1-n) CX, with zero encoded oracle calls. These are exact-real ideal-circuit semantics, not efficient table access, finite-bit angle evaluation or compiled complexity. The same decoder's actual addendum matched these 45 roots and found 40 additional owned constants for this module. Across all three modules it independently decoded 57 explicit roots plus 47 additional owned constants, 104 total, with the stated kernel/elaboration, axiom, provider and resource boundaries retained. This is a late opaque-digest association of that existing reconstruction, not a new blind run or approval of natural-source repairs.",
